.TH Edith 1 "2026-10-20" "edith 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
edith \- a friendly text editor for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B edith
.RB [ \-n | \-r ]
.RB [ \-o | \-O | \-p ]
.RB [ \-\-vim ]
.RB [ \-\-lang=\fICODE\fR ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.RI [ file " ...]"
.br
.B edith
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version " | " \-\-ts\-check
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B edith
is a text editor for the terminal with pull\-down menus, dialogs and mouse support, split
windows and tabs, syntax highlighting with tree\-sitter for more than 50 languages, code
formatting and an optional Vim mode.
.PP
F1 shows the key bindings, F10 or Alt opens the menu bar. Files that do not exist are
created when they are saved. Several files are opened in tabs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Show line numbers.
.TP
.B \-r
Show line numbers relative to the cursor line.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-O
Open several files in windows above each other / side by side.
.TP
.B \-p
Open several files in tabs (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-vim
Start with the Vim key bindings (Options > Vim Mode).
.TP
.BI \-\-lang= CODE
The language of the user interface:
.BR en ", " de ", " fr ", " es ", " it ", " hu " or " pl .
.TP
.B \-\-
End of the options: all following arguments are file names.
.TP
.B \-\-ts\-check
Load every compiled\-in tree\-sitter grammar and query and report problems.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
.TS
l l.
Ctrl+N, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Q	new, open, save, exit
Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y	undo, redo
Ctrl+X, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V, Ctrl+A	cut, copy, paste (system clipboard), select all
Ctrl+F, F3, Ctrl+R, Ctrl+G	find, find next, replace, go to line (also with regular expressions)
Shift+movement	select text
Tab, Shift+Tab	indent, unindent the selected lines
F8	reformat code
F6, Shift+F6, Ctrl+W	next window, previous window, close window
Ctrl+T, F4, Ctrl+PgDn, Ctrl+PgUp	new tab, close tab, next tab, previous tab
F12	Vim mode on and off
F1	help
F10, Alt	menu bar
Alt+letter	open a menu, choose a menu entry
h j k l	arrow keys in menus and dialogs (not in input fields)
Alt+Backspace	delete the word before the cursor
.TE
.PP
On macOS also: Option+Left/Right (word), Cmd+Left/Right (start/end of the line),
Cmd+Up/Down (start/end of the file), Option+Backspace, Cmd+Backspace (delete the word,
everything before the cursor in the line). In terminals that pass the Command key on, Cmd
works like Ctrl, and Cmd+Shift+Z redoes, Cmd+G finds the next match, Cmd+L goes to a line,
Cmd+Option+F replaces, Cmd+Shift+] and Cmd+Shift+[ switch to the next and previous tab.
.SH CLIPBOARD
Cut, copy and paste use the system clipboard: on macOS through
.BR pbcopy " and " pbpaste ,
on Linux through
.BR wl\-copy " and " wl\-paste ,
.BR xclip " or " xsel
when one of them is installed. Without them, and over SSH, paste asks the terminal for the
clipboard (OSC 52) and otherwise uses Edith's own clipboard. Copied text is also sent to the
terminal with OSC 52.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR LANGUAGE ", " LC_ALL ", " LC_MESSAGES ", " LANG
Select the language of the user interface (English for unknown locales).
.TP
.B COLORTERM
Values containing
.B truecolor
or
.B 24bit
enable 24\-bit colors.
.TP
.B EDITH_COLORS
.B 16
forces 16 colors,
.B 24
forces 24\-bit colors.
.TP
.B ESCDELAY
Milliseconds to wait after Esc for the rest of an escape sequence (default 30); raise it on
slow connections if keys like the arrows arrive as Esc and letters.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Directory of the configuration (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/edith/formatters
The formatter for each language used by Reformat Code, one line per language. The command is
run with
.I /bin/sh
in the file's directory, with the text on its standard input; Edith reads the result from its
standard output. Formatters run only for Reformat Code; some read project configuration that
is itself code (such as
.IR prettier.config.js ),
so do not reformat files of projects you do not trust.
.RS
.PP
.nf
# language = command  ({file} = the file name, {tabwidth} = the tab width)
Python = black \-q \-\-stdin\-filename {file} \-
JSON = builtin
Rust = none
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when no terminal is available, 2 for invalid options.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vim (1)
.PP
The README and the help dialog (F1) describe all features.
